From: plastron
Subject: [PATCH] PX30 (GKD Pixel 2): a charger's start boots to the charging screen

A charger plugged into the Pixel 2 while it is off makes the RK817 power it
on with the plug-in bit in ON_SOURCE. ROCKNIX's config turned it straight
off again (ROCKCHIP_RK8XX_DISABLE_BOOT_ON_POWERON), so the screen stayed
dark while it charged. That option is off now (px2.config), and the board's
late init sets zy_charge=1 instead, which boot.scr turns into zycharge=1 on
the kernel's line: ZyperOS shows its charging screen. A restart has its own
bit in ON_SOURCE (0x02 on the device, the charger's 0x40), so it never looks
like a charger's start.
---
--- a/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/go2.c
+++ b/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/go2.c
@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@
 #include <dm.h>
 #include <env.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
+#include <power/pmic.h>
+#include <power/rk8xx_pmic.h>
 
 #define DTB_DIR			"rockchip/"
 
@@ -101,10 +103,36 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * plastron: a charger plugged into the GKD Pixel 2 while it is off makes the
+ * RK817 power it on, and its ON_SOURCE says so: the plug-in bit, not the
+ * power key's. U-Boot turned it straight off again for that
+ * (ROCKCHIP_RK8XX_DISABLE_BOOT_ON_POWERON, off in px2.config now); instead
+ * the boot goes on with zy_charge=1, which boot.scr puts on the kernel's line
+ * as zycharge=1, and ZyperOS shows its charging screen (its DESIGN.md 11.25)
+ * rather than the boot animation and the home. A restart is a reason of its
+ * own there (0x02, read on a Pixel 2 on 2026-11-06, against 0x40 for the
+ * charger), so one never comes back as a charger's start.
+ */
+static void px2_charge_boot(void)
+{
+	struct udevice *pmic;
+	int on;
+
+	if (uclass_get_device_by_driver(UCLASS_PMIC, DM_DRIVER_GET(rockchip_rk805), &pmic))
+		return;
+	on = pmic_reg_read(pmic, RK817_ON_SOURCE);
+	if (on < 0 || !(on & RK8XX_ON_PLUG_IN) || (on & RK8XX_ON_PWRON))
+		return;
+	printf("Started by a charger: zy_charge=1\n");
+	env_set("zy_charge", "1");
+}
+
 int rk_board_late_init(void)
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	px2_charge_boot();
 	ret = oga_detect_device();
 	if (ret) {
 		printf("Unable to detect device type: %d\n", ret);
